{
  "title": "'Customize with AI': rename it and run it on a frontier model (Opus 5.5)",
  "description": "'Customize with AI' (iOS CustomEnrichSheet.swift and RecipeDetailView menu, web aiOperations.ts customEnrich, server POST /api/enrich/custom, core ramekin-core/src/ai/custom_enrich.rs) runs on AiConfig.model, the shared DEFAULT_MODEL google/gemini-3.8-flash used for tags, titles and descriptions. \
It should use a true frontier model: anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 (already DEFAULT_INGREDIENT_MODEL via OpenRouter). (1) Give it its own model setting (e.g. DEFAULT_CUSTOMIZE_MODEL and RAMEKIN_AI_CUSTOMIZE_MODEL, like the extraction model), defaulting to anthropic/claude-opus-5.5, and rerun `make ai-eval SUITE=custom-enrich` so data/ai-evals/custom-enrich.md records Opus's results and cost next to the old default. (2) Latency: CUSTOM_ENRICH_TIMEOUT_SECS is 50 s to fit the clients' 60 s request timeout, and Opus writing out a whole recipe may not fit. \
Measure; if it doesn't fit, run it as a background job the clients poll (the scrape-job pattern), which customize-2 needs anyway. (3) Rename it on both clients and through the code (custom_enrich, CustomEnrichRequest, /api/enrich/custom, the prompt name). \
Candidates: 'Edit with AI…', 'Ask AI to change…', 'Adapt with AI…'. \
Recommendation: 'Edit with AI…', since it changes the recipe the way the user describes, and it stops colliding with the enrich/normalize naming in normalize-1. \
No data/ diffs expected beyond the ai-eval results file.",
